e gates passed project-wide, but neither is a per-changed-line fact for this file. The test evidence: keybindings-menu-test.sh passed in a current report (68 passed, 0 failed), and 4MKB's requirement-level claim is observed_pass. The 17 tests the PR adds (lines 285-637) drive dispatch_lua_function_binding through a stubbed `hyprctl` that runs the dispatched Lua.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":676},{"id":"test/shell.d/keybindings-menu-test.sh","kind":"test"},{"id":"code_mcdc_coverage","kind":"check"},{"id":"SW-REQ-261005-4MKB","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"medium","title":"Changed-line coverage of bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings was not measured","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"On the evaluated tree I extracted the PR's functions the way its test does and drove them with its stub_hyprctl_dispatch (macOS, luajit as lua). Results: one matching bind with ref 264 gives exit 0 and calls 264. Two binds with the same identity, a non-numeric ref, a reload between lookup and call, and the same chord and description in another submap each give exit 1, call nothing, and leave no mark. The picked-row awk: two identical exec rows dispatch the first, as before. An exec row and a `__lua` row that read the same give no record. A label containing `\\t` matches through ENVIRON but not through the base's `awk -v`. In our Linux runs, keybindings-menu-test.sh passed 33/33 on the PR head and on its merge onto quattro 035ce29f, and 16/16 on quattro. These results are outside the package.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":660},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":672},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":762}],"severity":"info","title":"Opinion (my own run): the dispatch path calls exactly the one matching bind and l