f the upstream PR. Commit dc773390 makes its stub print `arg: 264` for the Select all bind, the shape Hyprland 0.56.2 prints. With the old empty `arg:` a fix that dispatches through the ref still read as broken. Its hyprctl() stub is untraced and the file is out of scope (changed_files_out_of_scope). It realizes the KI's check on 0W96, so no product requirement is missing.","refs":[{"id":"pocs/crs-260930-jvx8-c02.sh","kind":"file","line":30},{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-FUNC-BIND-NO-DISPATCH.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-0W96","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"The reproducer change is our proof work, outside the verification scope","verification":{"evidence":[{"id":"pocs/crs-260930-jvx8-c02.sh:hyprctl","kind":"file","line":30}],"method":"review.scope (changed units, intent graph, spec-gap candidates): units","note":"pocs/crs-260930-jvx8-c02.sh:hyprctl (modified) is traced to no requirement. The author's position (intended) is judgement, not verified; a human decision settles it.","status":"confirmed"}},{"detail":"80236345 sets the KI's status to fixed by omacom/omarchy#11851. 49ebebcf re-captures its evidence as not reproduced. In our Linux runs the fixed reproducer exits 0 (defect present) on quattro-proof 1e433732 and exits 1 (fixed) on the PR head and its merge.","refs":[{"id":"proof/known-issues/KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-FUNC-BIND-NO-DISPATCH.yaml","kind":"file","line":1},{"id":"pocs/crs-260930-jvx8-c02.sh","kind":"file","line":14},{"id":"SW-REQ-260922-0W96","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"KI-MENU-KEYBINDINGS-FUNC-BIND-NO-DISPATCH is marked fixed on the mirror (proof work)","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"The PR text lists Zoom in, Reset zoom and the three universal clipboard actions. The base also ships `Select all` (default/hypr/bindings/clipboard.lua:45, `send_shortcut_once(\"CTRL\", \"A\")`), a Lua function bind next to them. The fix is generic, so it covers that bind too; the reproducer uses it.","refs":[{"id":"default/hypr/bindings/clipboard.lua","kind":"file","line":45},{"id":"default/hypr/bindings/utilities.lua","kind":"file","line":124},{"id":"SW-REQ-261005-4MKB","kind":"requirement"}],"severity":"info","title":"Opinion (reading): six shipped binds are affected at this base, not five","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}},{"detail":"review.effects is absent for this bash change, so no new_call_path, effect_gain or new_mutable_state claim can be checked, and the scope analysis could not detect uncodified connections. From reading: the new callees are dispatch_lua_expression (existing; runs `hyprctl dispatch`) and `hyprctl binds`, `base64` and awk. The only product caller of dispatch_binding is the script's own main block (line 767). These facts come from reading, not from the engine.","refs":[{"id":"review.effects.approximations","kind":"check"},{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":767}],"severity":"info","title":"Change effects were not analyzed (effects_unavailable): no call-level facts","verification":{"evidence":[],"method":"untyped finding","note":"No typed claim: this finding is the author's judgement and is not checked against the package.","status":"unverifiable"}}],"packageDigest":"sha256:dd47c0fbb1c8c463427055a6ed000d64a973354c13127255e387080f77d6a7e3","packageIdentity":"epkg-1ed1a3975417539a0c8691fd37bffa994bf525791845385d528101180947d3f8","riskAssessment":{"level":"medium","rationale":"A targeted fix. Its tests drive the new dispatch path through a stubbed hyprctl that runs the Lua, and they cover refusal on reload, ambiguity and bad refs. But changed-line coverage of the script was not measured, nothing ran against a live compositor, and the configured differential does not reach this script. Two compat findings (witness renames from an engine parsing artefact) prevent readiness until a reviewer decides. Rebinds that keep the shipped chord and description still run the shipped action without #7564. Advisory only."},"schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-annotation.v1","suggestedTests":[{"forClaim":12,"rationale":"Settles whether `hl.dispatch(registry[ref])` runs the function in a real compositor and leaves no mark, including a `hyprctl reload` between two picks. All package tests stub hyprctl.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":672}],"title":"Live Hyprland 0.56.2: pick Reset zoom and Zoom in from Super+K"},{"forClaim":13,"rationale":"Pick `File manager` after `o.rebind(\"SUPER + SHIFT + F\", \"File manager\", { launch = \"flea\" })` and assert flea is launched. Fails on this head (the cached shipped expression wins). Passes with #7564 also applied.","refs":[{"id":"bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings","kind":"file","line":318}],"title":"Rebind keeping the shipped chord and description runs the user's action"},{"forClaim":14,"rationale":"Append `error(\"a personal module that fails to load\")` and `o.bind(\"SUPER + ALT + P\", \"Personal bind\", \"true\")` to the user's bindings.lua, report it as `__lua` with ref 300, pick it, and assert ref 300 was called. Uses the PR's stub_hyprctl_dispatch, lua_function_bind, pick_from_menu and called helpers. Our run: passes on this head (34/34) and fails with quattro's script.","refs":[{"id":"test/shell.d/keybindings-menu-test.sh","kind":"file","line":374}],"title":"A bind declared after a config error is called through its ref"}],"summary":"**What the PR does.** Upstream #11851 (vdvoorder) makes `Super + K` run Lua function binds. Before, picking one exited 1 and ran nothing. Hyprland reports them as `__lua` with a registry ref. When the source replay has no expression for such a bind, the row now stores the bind's identity: mask, submap, key, keycode and description, base64-encoded (dynamic_bindings, line 322). On a pick, the script writes a mark in the Lua registry and re-reads `hyprctl binds`. If exactly one bind matches and its ref is numeric, it calls `registry[ref]`, but only while the mark is still there. The picked row is now matched through `ENVIRON`, not `awk -v`. The cache key moves from v14 to v19. On the mirror that is commit e03ad1ea. Every later commit is our proof work: a reproducer fixture fix, KI status, SW-REQ-261005-4MKB, 3 test scenarios, 2 test-harness fixes, obligation tags, `mcdc:ignore` lines and trace reviews.\n\n**Is the fix verified?** Changed-line coverage was not measured for bin/omarchy-menu-keybindings (coverage_unmeasured), so the package has no coverage fact for it. Test report: 68 passed, 0 failed, current. The error_handling cells of 4MKB and 9DMS are observed_pass; joined via tags on the one file-level test. My stubbed run of the dispatch path calls ref 264 for one matching bind. It calls nothing for two matches, a non-numeric ref, a reload between lookup and call, or another submap.\n\n**Compatibility.** compat reports 2 mcdc_diff findings: cf-4c5e34efd4c84e91 (0W96) and cf-8507c81c0f32c95a (9DMS). Both prevent readiness; only a reviewer can approve them. Each is the same witness renamed. A Lua `type(action)` line in the PR's test heredoc is read as a function name, so the witness `keybindings-menu-test.sh:1` became `type`. Same file, line 1, scenarios 1-3, meets policy. An engine parsing artefact. The differential's 0 differences come from a harness that runs only Menu.qml/MenuModel.js. Readiness: not_assessed. Next decision: human_judgement (compat_changes_unapproved), by a reviewer. Nothing here is an approval.\n\n**Questions for a human.** (1) Does it run under a live Hyprland? All tests are stubbed. (2) A rebind that keeps the shipped chord and description still runs the shipped action; #7564 fixes that half. (3) Should a test pin binds the replay never reaches?\n\n**Traceability.** 4MKB and 0W96 match at function level, 9DMS only at file level. Change effects were not analyzed.\n\n**Not caused by this PR.** No check failed; 13 were skipped by configuration."}
